mpler: read as before into Body *bodies_in, then for i loop assign arrays.\n- After simulation, create Body *out = malloc(n*sizeof(Body)); fill from SoA; write out.\n\nBut that adds extra memory copies O(n) which is negligible compared to O(n^2). Could also use fwrite with a custom packing loop writing each body individually? That would be many small writes; better pack into buffer.\n\nAlternatively, we could keep the Body struct but reorder loops? But SoA is key for vectorization and cache. We'll do SoA.\n\nNow implement body_force as:\n\nvoid body_force(float *px, float *py, float *pz, float *vx, float *vy, float *vz, int n, float dt) {\n  const int IB = 8; // block size\n  #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n  for (int ib = 0; ib < n; ib += IB) {\n    int iend = ib + IB;\n    if (iend > n) iend = n;\n    float fx[IB], fy[IB], fz[IB];\n    // initialize accumulators\n    for (int k=0; k<iend-ib; ++k) { fx[k]=fy[k]=fz[k]=0.0f; }\n    // loop over all j\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n      float pjx = px[j];\n      float pjy = py[j];\n      float pjz = pz[j];\n      for (int i=ib, k=0; i<iend; ++i,++k) {\n        float dx = pjx - px[i];\n        float dy = pjy - py[i];\n        float dz = pjz - pz[i];\n        float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n        float inv_dist = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n        float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n        fx[k] += dx * inv_dist3;\n        fy[k] += dy * inv_dist3;\n        fz[k] += dz * inv_dist3;\n      }\n    }\n    // update velocities\n    for (int i=ib, k=0; i<iend; ++i,++k) {\n      vx[i] += dt*fx[k];\n      vy[i] += dt*fy[k];\n      vz[i] += dt*fz[k];\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nThis preserves per-i j order exactly: for each i in block, the inner loop over k processes j sequentially from 0..n-1. The accumulation into fx[k] happens in same order as baseline (j increasing). So bit-exact.\n\nPotential issue: OpenMP parallelization over blocks may cause different threads to execute blocks;